WEBVTT

00:19.100 --> 00:21.210
Hey, Hyoma!

00:22.830 --> 00:24.330
Were you waiting long?

00:24.330 --> 00:25.670
H-Haori?!

00:25.670 --> 00:27.760
Y-You...

00:27.760 --> 00:30.550
Wh-Why are you dressed like that?!

00:31.110 --> 00:34.280
You're dressed in your usual style, I see.

00:34.280 --> 00:36.910
Appearances are so important 
for these things.

00:36.910 --> 00:38.840
You should really step it up.

00:38.840 --> 00:40.060
You're my boyfriend, aren't you?

00:40.440 --> 00:42.330
And we're heading out on a date.

00:43.530 --> 00:45.230
Come along, now.

00:45.230 --> 00:46.560
Oh, I know...

00:46.880 --> 00:48.320
Let's hold hands!

00:52.660 --> 00:53.670
<i>What...</i>

00:54.190 --> 00:55.820
<i>What in the world...</i>

00:56.280 --> 00:58.090
<i>have I gotten myself into?!</i>

01:07.910 --> 01:15.670
<i>Malevolent Spirits</i>

02:29.000 --> 02:34.000
<b>Botan</b>

02:34.710 --> 02:36.960
<b>30 Minutes Earlier</b>

02:37.440 --> 02:39.470
I'm back!

02:40.370 --> 02:41.930
Welcome back, Haori!

02:41.930 --> 02:44.320
Kagami... tea, please.

02:44.320 --> 02:45.420
Sure thing.

02:45.420 --> 02:46.980
Where's Kushige?

02:49.860 --> 02:52.270
Anything happen while we were gone?

02:52.270 --> 02:57.690
Well... Hyoma-san got 
grilled by Aogi yesterday.

02:58.480 --> 03:00.200
I had a feeling.

03:00.640 --> 03:03.200
But we made it through safe and sound!

03:03.200 --> 03:05.580
I don't think there was 
anything else weird...

03:05.580 --> 03:06.700
Nagatsuki-san!

03:09.500 --> 03:11.210
I must know more about you!

03:11.210 --> 03:13.580
Would you kindly go out with me?!

03:15.810 --> 03:17.450
I'm sorry to spring this on you suddenly.

03:17.450 --> 03:20.970
But this is an extremely 
urgent matter for me.

03:24.060 --> 03:25.990
Well? Do you agree?

03:29.800 --> 03:31.770
P-Palm strike...

03:31.770 --> 03:34.300
I'm sorry, Hyoma-san...

03:34.730 --> 03:38.570
I have to hand in this report by 4:00 today!

03:38.570 --> 03:40.400
I've lost two nights' sleep over it!

03:40.400 --> 03:41.990
So I gotta go!

03:42.540 --> 03:43.990
Welcome home, Haori!

03:45.240 --> 03:47.120
T-Take care out there.

03:48.040 --> 03:49.190
What was that?

03:53.280 --> 03:58.180
That "Aogi" said that Nagatsuki-san 
was a "yorimashi."

03:59.210 --> 04:04.130
I believe it is necessary for me to 
ascertain the meaning of this term.

04:04.130 --> 04:07.960
So you wanted to "go out" 
to ask Botan more about it?

04:07.960 --> 04:11.770
It really sounded like 
you were hitting on her.

04:11.770 --> 04:14.520
Yes. The way he spoke...

04:15.150 --> 04:17.200
He made it sound like there was 
something about Nagatsuki-san

04:17.200 --> 04:20.540
that fundamentally attracts the inhuman.

04:22.170 --> 04:25.830
As a Saenome, I feel it 
is crucial to protect her.

04:26.720 --> 04:29.870
If there's a reason she's under threat, 
I must know what it is.

04:30.360 --> 04:32.860
Wh-What should we do, Haori?

04:41.120 --> 04:42.630
Very well.

04:43.330 --> 04:44.720
We can tell him?

04:44.720 --> 04:47.890
He's not acting out of mere curiosity.

04:48.190 --> 04:51.420
Besides, we'd have to tell him eventually.

04:51.420 --> 04:52.730
We're just speeding up the timeline.

04:53.080 --> 04:54.760
Leave this to me.

04:57.620 --> 05:00.120
Hyoma-san, prepare for an outing.

05:01.780 --> 05:03.770
I need to fix up my makeup.

05:03.770 --> 05:06.360
Would you meet me in front 
of the convenience store?

05:06.920 --> 05:09.120
We'll be going on a date together!

05:12.660 --> 05:13.590
What?

05:15.340 --> 05:19.630
Honestly... I was wondering 
what your game was.

05:20.200 --> 05:21.820
So this is it, eh?

05:25.170 --> 05:26.880
Hurry! She's turning!

05:26.880 --> 05:28.550
Keep your distance, Haori!

05:32.350 --> 05:35.750
Aren't we less conspicuous 
if we look like a couple?

05:36.400 --> 05:39.190
I'm not especially comfortable 
with any of this.

05:43.620 --> 05:45.240
But I need to ask...

05:45.240 --> 05:47.530
What even is the point of 
tailing her like this?

05:48.550 --> 05:51.720
The first thing I need you to witness

05:51.720 --> 05:54.120
is the world in which she finds herself,

05:54.120 --> 05:56.830
the scenery of her everyday life.

05:58.200 --> 06:02.340
Kushige's barrier encompasses the 
territory of the Nagatsuki estate.

06:02.840 --> 06:06.720
The barrier keeps many things out.

06:08.600 --> 06:11.390
Speaking of which, is Kushige still out?

06:17.880 --> 06:21.650
But when she leaves the mansion, 
in the outside world...

06:22.300 --> 06:23.210
Go on.

06:23.210 --> 06:26.030
Perk up your senses, 
and I think you'll notice it.

06:26.320 --> 06:27.480
You should be able to.

06:36.530 --> 06:38.070
<i>What in the world...</i>

06:38.800 --> 06:44.360
<i>The presences... no, the gazes... 
of so many tsukumogami...</i>

06:45.180 --> 06:47.400
<i>They're all focused on Nagatsuki-san?!</i>

06:48.680 --> 06:50.920
<i>Not from any one direction, either.</i>

06:51.390 --> 06:52.810
<i>From all around her!</i>

06:53.260 --> 06:54.140
Damn it!

06:54.140 --> 06:54.990
Nagatsuki-sa—

06:54.990 --> 06:56.480
Stop!

06:56.480 --> 06:58.440
Calm down, Hyoma.

06:58.440 --> 07:00.640
They're just watching.

07:01.150 --> 07:03.950
Breaths held, presences masked,

07:03.950 --> 07:06.280
they watch Botan, but go no further...

07:08.640 --> 07:10.620
They won't harm her.

07:10.620 --> 07:13.220
And she's aware of their eyes on her, as well.

07:15.030 --> 07:16.730
It's always been this way.

07:17.200 --> 07:19.690
She accepts it for what it is.

07:20.120 --> 07:21.340
Didn't I tell you?

07:22.590 --> 07:26.570
This is the scenery of Botan's daily life.

07:26.570 --> 07:28.150
That can't be...

07:28.830 --> 07:31.400
If you can't take that much on faith,

07:31.400 --> 07:34.430
then telling you any more is pointless.

07:35.090 --> 07:37.620
If you wish to know more, 
then trust what I say.

07:41.190 --> 07:42.810
You're right.

07:43.430 --> 07:44.970
Of course.

07:50.400 --> 07:52.070
<b>Report Turn-In Box</b>

07:54.530 --> 07:55.820
What's the time?

07:56.330 --> 07:57.580
Yes!

07:57.580 --> 08:00.350
Th-Thank goodness!

08:00.350 --> 08:03.130
I made it just in time...

08:04.160 --> 08:05.380
Bon-chan!

08:06.760 --> 08:08.590
Kei... Natsuki...

08:08.590 --> 08:11.100
What, just turning it in now?

08:11.540 --> 08:13.970
You're usually more put-together 
than that, Bon-chan!

08:14.360 --> 08:17.320
Well... My life's been pretty eventful lately.

08:17.320 --> 08:19.340
It's got me kind of distracted.

08:19.340 --> 08:21.120
Eventful <i>how</i>, I wonder?

08:21.120 --> 08:22.620
Distracted by <i>what</i>?

08:22.620 --> 08:26.730
A handsome new boyfriend, perhaps?

08:27.310 --> 08:29.320
A handsome...

08:30.040 --> 08:30.890
No, no, no!

08:30.890 --> 08:32.660
Of course not!

08:33.180 --> 08:34.990
I can't even imagine...

08:35.370 --> 08:40.280
<i>Wait, wasn't Hyoma-san 
saying something earlier?</i>

08:40.280 --> 08:41.290
Nagatsuki-san!

08:42.330 --> 08:46.630
<i>I m-might be remembering wrong... 
but he seemed pretty close to me!</i>

08:46.630 --> 08:48.800
<i>D-Darn it!</i>

08:48.800 --> 08:50.970
Yeah, I definitely have questions.

08:51.540 --> 08:53.130
Spill your guts!

08:53.130 --> 08:56.650
It's nothing! I mean it!

09:00.380 --> 09:06.770
A tsukumogami is born when a marebito 
possesses an object to serve as its vessel.

09:07.670 --> 09:10.040
The word "marebito" originally referred to

09:10.040 --> 09:15.550
a visiting god bringing blessings 
from a foreign land.

09:15.550 --> 09:18.160
And in a way, we do have 
a sort of divine power.

09:18.160 --> 09:22.200
What else would you call the ability to 
give life and new form to inanimate objects?

09:23.730 --> 09:25.020
Fair enough.

09:26.850 --> 09:28.970
You can also look at it this way.

09:29.400 --> 09:33.670
"'Tsukumogami' is the state of 
being blessed by the marebito."

09:34.190 --> 09:37.550
There was a person who took 
this idea to its logical conclusion...

09:37.920 --> 09:42.060
"What if a marebito chose 
a different receptacle?"

09:42.510 --> 09:45.130
For instance... a human?

09:46.190 --> 09:50.160
A marebito can bring so much power 
to even the most disposable of things.

09:50.160 --> 09:51.940
What if one were to dwell within a human?

09:51.940 --> 09:55.360
Would they not receive even greater power?

09:55.360 --> 09:59.820
Would they become a living god that 
brings its blessings to the land of the living?

10:00.550 --> 10:04.540
And there was a person who 
decided to put that to the test.

10:08.280 --> 10:09.830
The word "yorimashi" refers to

10:10.660 --> 10:12.590
a human possessed by a god.

10:15.430 --> 10:21.510
Botan carries within her a marebito, 
just as we tsukumogami do.

10:22.440 --> 10:23.970
It's so cold!

10:24.330 --> 10:26.340
It hasn't yet awakened.

10:27.780 --> 10:30.100
But it is there.

10:31.320 --> 10:35.740
All who learn of this inevitably seek a way

10:35.740 --> 10:39.860
to turn Botan's still-uncertain 
blessings to their own advantage.

10:39.860 --> 10:42.940
Whether they be tsukumogami... or human.

10:44.410 --> 10:47.580
If any one of them were to 
approach Botan for that purpose,

10:47.580 --> 10:49.190
it would be a free-for-all, wouldn't it?

10:49.870 --> 10:52.970
Hence the shared law—

10:53.800 --> 10:57.010
"Don't make use of Nagatsuki Botan."

10:53.880 --> 10:57.010
<b>Don't make use of Nagatsuki Botan</b>

10:57.630 --> 11:00.090
None may actually approach her.

11:00.470 --> 11:03.430
Hence why they all merely 
bide their time, watching.

11:04.430 --> 11:09.640
Of course, there's a lot of behind-the-scenes 
finagling to keep everyone in check.

11:09.640 --> 11:10.820
I see.

11:11.400 --> 11:15.720
If you speak the truth, it explains 
much of what Aogi said.

11:13.230 --> 11:17.960
If it's true, it means 
they broke the rules first.

11:17.960 --> 11:22.520
It'll mean all-out war breaking out 
among us for Nagatsuki Botan.

11:23.610 --> 11:26.430
And now, let me ask this...

11:26.430 --> 11:28.120
Where does this leave all of you?

11:29.280 --> 11:32.500
Can you swear to me that your proximity 
to Nagatsuki-san has no ulterior motive?

11:32.890 --> 11:34.630
Tell me, Haori!

11:39.660 --> 11:40.860
You cut your hair?

11:40.860 --> 11:41.920
Looks cute!

11:41.920 --> 11:43.220
Thanks!

11:44.660 --> 11:45.930
Nagatsuki-san.

11:46.600 --> 11:48.060
She...

11:49.150 --> 11:50.730
Botan-chan...

11:51.330 --> 11:54.730
Sometimes I catch her just standing there,
staring into the distance

11:54.730 --> 11:56.540
as if she's looking at something.

11:58.230 --> 12:01.300
And whenever that happens...

12:03.300 --> 12:06.540
Any children who are with her 
suddenly become frightened.

12:07.400 --> 12:09.860
When I ask them what's wrong, they say...

12:13.860 --> 12:15.500
"It's so creepy."

12:16.050 --> 12:19.300
"I feel like there are all 
these eyes watching me."

12:22.800 --> 12:26.260
As a teacher, I feel bad saying this,

12:26.870 --> 12:30.920
but Botan-chan has this 
unapproachable aura about her...

12:43.490 --> 12:44.500
Botan.

12:47.490 --> 12:49.530
Come on. Let's go home.

12:55.170 --> 12:56.370
<i>Okay.</i>

12:59.130 --> 13:04.760
Can I swear that our proximity 
to Botan has no ulterior motive?

13:04.760 --> 13:05.840
Yes.

13:10.600 --> 13:14.440
That's a ridiculous question.

13:14.440 --> 13:15.580
Don't ask it again.

13:19.560 --> 13:22.150
We've watched her all this time.

13:23.320 --> 13:25.610
She was left in our care,

13:26.080 --> 13:30.150
and for the first three years, 
until the aforementioned law propagated,

13:30.590 --> 13:33.240
she was not allowed to leave the estate.

13:35.330 --> 13:38.120
When she was finally allowed outside...

13:38.650 --> 13:42.810
Children, who naturally possess 
a strong sixth sense, avoided her.

13:43.290 --> 13:47.510
Adults, seeing how their children acted, 
also gave her a wide berth.

13:50.540 --> 13:52.840
The only ones who would draw near...

13:53.820 --> 13:57.290
were those drawn to her 
marebito's power—be they human

13:58.480 --> 14:00.020
or monster.

14:23.960 --> 14:25.510
As we watched over her,

14:26.180 --> 14:29.180
a feeling began to take root within us.

14:32.690 --> 14:37.240
Not merely our feelings 
as her bridal trousseau...

14:37.980 --> 14:41.320
But a kind of... parental love, I believe.

14:44.420 --> 14:48.760
It took years for her to be able to go out 
without minding the eyes watching her.

14:49.570 --> 14:54.410
More years for her peers to 
become numb to those eyes.

14:55.650 --> 15:00.600
And still more years for her to 
be able to enjoy life with a smile.

15:03.880 --> 15:06.420
We have watched her all this time.

15:07.240 --> 15:09.170
Ulterior motives?

15:10.450 --> 15:13.420
I can say with confidence that we have none.

15:20.480 --> 15:23.320
Oh? You still have doubts?

15:24.170 --> 15:25.860
You know...

15:25.860 --> 15:30.780
Zohei-san has already given his 
approval for us to stay with Botan.

15:31.230 --> 15:35.020
Are you questioning the judgment 
of the head of House Kunato?

15:35.690 --> 15:37.780
Maybe I should tell him that.

15:42.610 --> 15:44.750
Well? What now?

15:46.680 --> 15:48.350
That's the entire story.

15:48.350 --> 15:51.260
You understand the position 
she's in now, don't you?

15:51.560 --> 15:54.890
If you think she's more 
trouble than she's worth,

15:55.320 --> 15:58.220
no one will object to you 
returning to House Kunato.

16:01.080 --> 16:02.940
That thought never entered my mind.

16:03.450 --> 16:06.800
If I return now, I'll be exiled from the Saenome.

16:06.800 --> 16:09.360
Then I'll never achieve my goal.

16:10.690 --> 16:11.770
And...

16:13.480 --> 16:14.650
I will...

16:16.080 --> 16:18.230
I will protect her.

16:18.960 --> 16:21.540
From the moment I deemed that a necessity,

16:21.540 --> 16:23.100
leaving ceased to be an option.

16:27.200 --> 16:29.550
Yes. You can say that, can't you?

16:31.510 --> 16:34.800
See? He took it very well, didn't he,

16:34.800 --> 16:35.910
Kagami?

16:38.730 --> 16:39.600
Yeah.

16:39.600 --> 16:41.980
I followed along because I was worried, but...

16:44.890 --> 16:46.690
I-I'm so glad!

16:49.230 --> 16:52.830
It's no wonder you're Botan's future husband!

16:52.830 --> 16:53.790
Exactly!

16:53.790 --> 16:54.830
What?!

16:55.100 --> 16:55.900
Wait!

16:55.900 --> 16:57.740
I-Is that what this was about?

16:57.740 --> 17:00.750
"I will protect her" 
means marriage, doesn't it?

17:00.750 --> 17:01.450
No!

17:02.680 --> 17:04.480
Don't be so shy, dear!

17:04.480 --> 17:05.450
Yeah!

17:05.450 --> 17:06.940
I'm telling you, I didn't—

17:06.940 --> 17:09.400
Huh? You guys!

17:10.300 --> 17:13.090
What are you all doing out here?

17:15.370 --> 17:16.410
Botan?!

17:16.840 --> 17:18.300
Wh-When did you get here?

17:18.300 --> 17:22.810
Well... I turned in my report, 
and now I'm heading home.

17:22.810 --> 17:25.370
O-Oh! Did you make the deadline?

17:26.240 --> 17:27.730
Right at the buzzer.

17:27.730 --> 17:29.880
So, what's going on?

17:29.880 --> 17:31.580
U-Um...

17:31.580 --> 17:34.520
J-Just a little get-together!

17:36.360 --> 17:37.840
Why are you dressed like that?

17:37.840 --> 17:39.390
For the get-together!

17:40.620 --> 17:42.120
A get-together? Here?

17:42.120 --> 17:44.830
They have the best sweet dumplings!

17:42.820 --> 17:43.820
Kagami.

17:44.830 --> 17:47.240
That's true... but something 
still seems fishy here.

17:44.850 --> 17:46.790
I haven't had the opportunity to ask...

17:47.240 --> 17:49.500
Nothing's fishy at all!

17:47.310 --> 17:49.500
Nagatsuki-san's parents...

17:49.930 --> 17:53.140
Has she no close relatives 
who would offer her aid?

17:55.460 --> 17:58.200
We don't know anything about her parents.

17:58.200 --> 18:01.390
Her grandfather was taking care 
of her when we first met her.

18:01.800 --> 18:07.770
When he died, there was someone who 
came to visit Botan, worried about her...

18:08.480 --> 18:14.200
But that helping hand never reached her.

18:15.880 --> 18:18.780
She's seriously been through a lot.

18:21.440 --> 18:24.330
She still carries deep scars on her heart.

18:24.890 --> 18:27.040
And yet she still...

18:29.250 --> 18:30.090
I see.

18:31.600 --> 18:34.300
Nagatsuki-san is a strong person.

18:41.000 --> 18:43.440
It's gotten quite late.

18:43.440 --> 18:46.360
Well, you had your date and all.

18:46.360 --> 18:48.540
Please don't talk about that.

18:49.480 --> 18:54.110
What? You told Hyoma-san about my past?

18:54.110 --> 18:55.280
Yes.

18:55.280 --> 18:58.270
It relates to his area of 
specialization, after all,

18:58.270 --> 19:00.540
so I thought it best to inform him.

19:05.040 --> 19:06.490
What's the matter?

19:06.490 --> 19:10.090
It just makes me sound delusional, you know?!

19:10.090 --> 19:12.460
Like just the cringiest kind of nerd possible!

19:13.840 --> 19:16.670
<i>I sense the presence of the inhuman.</i>

19:16.670 --> 19:18.440
That kind of thing?

19:19.090 --> 19:21.830
But he really wanted to know.

19:22.290 --> 19:27.220
Also... did you forget that you hit him 
with a palm strike on the way out?

19:30.480 --> 19:31.430
Excuse me.

19:32.750 --> 19:34.250
Is something the matter?

19:37.490 --> 19:39.500
I'm so sorry!

19:39.500 --> 19:42.700
That palm strike... I... 
I didn't do it on purpose, I promise!

19:43.140 --> 19:44.600
Ah... well...

19:44.600 --> 19:47.580
I should have been more 
mindful of my words, as well.

19:48.600 --> 19:50.940
And, um...

19:50.940 --> 19:53.160
Haori told you, right?

19:54.230 --> 19:55.620
About my... situation.

20:00.080 --> 20:02.220
Yes. She did.

20:04.350 --> 20:05.480
She did.

20:06.310 --> 20:07.850
And if I may be honest...

20:10.020 --> 20:13.100
I was truly impressed, Nagatsuki-san!

20:18.880 --> 20:22.520
To bear up under hardship 
and carry on vibrantly...

20:22.520 --> 20:24.840
Well, it's not really...

20:24.840 --> 20:25.740
Huh?

20:26.160 --> 20:28.380
Isn't this where you're supposed to run off?

20:28.380 --> 20:30.250
To decide that I'm strange?

20:30.250 --> 20:32.310
I can think of no reason to do that.

20:32.800 --> 20:38.750
Though I will admit that I find your residency 
among tsukumogami to be unusual.

20:39.640 --> 20:42.060
You have mentioned that, yeah.

20:43.540 --> 20:44.600
So...

20:50.550 --> 20:53.780
It's true. It didn't change anything.

20:54.440 --> 20:58.340
You heard all that about me... 
and you were impressed?

21:01.460 --> 21:04.620
I've never gotten that reaction before.

21:06.210 --> 21:07.160
Yeah.

21:10.280 --> 21:12.660
It makes me happy, Hyoma-san.

21:20.930 --> 21:22.990
Er... well...

21:22.990 --> 21:25.110
Botan!

21:26.920 --> 21:28.010
I'm so happy!

21:28.010 --> 21:29.850
Isn't that nice, Botan?

21:29.850 --> 21:33.510
Hey! What's with you two?

21:52.200 --> 21:53.420
I see now.

23:24.960 --> 23:39.980
<b>Next Time</b>

23:24.960 --> 23:39.980
<b>Quickening</b>
